   "issue": "The 2026-10-29 edit rewrote clause 1 of AC-AT-106 so that a knob set one step outside its published safe range produces only an ADVISORY CI diff and 'boot does not refuse' (ADR-0007 s2.5). The same AC's cliff clause, the Tuning Knobs preamble ('Safe range is the range the lints of Formulas allow'; where a lint sets the edge it is computed at the ring-3 test row) and E-10 all say a lint-set edge refuses boot. For TAU_ATT_TICKS (1200 to 3600, and below 1817 at ring-3), TELL_DRAW_LO (876 edge, AC-AT-64), HOLD_PM, L_CEIL_PM, ATT_MARGIN and W_P, one step outside the range IS the F-15 / ring-1 lint failure, so it refuses boot with CONTENT_INVARIANT. A test written from clause 1 ('boot does not refuse') would fail against a correct implementation for those knobs. Formulas note 7 (L1828) is now stale in the same way: it takes negative fixtures 'from the first out-of-range row of Tuning Knobs', but an out-of-range row no longer fails anything unless a named invariant binds it.",
   "fix": "Split AC-AT-106 into two classes. (a) Knobs whose edge is set by a named invariant (the six cliff knobs and the ring-1 columns of Safe-ranges-by-row, plus TELL_DRAW_LO via AC-AT-64): one step outside refuses boot with CONTENT_INVARIANT. (b) All other knobs: one step outside gives only the ADVISORY CI diff, and boot does not refuse unless a schema bound (CONTENT_FIELD_RANGE) or an invariant fires. Reword Formulas note 7 to take negative fixtures from the first row whose edge is invariant-bound or schema-bound, not from any out-of-range row."
